{"id": "wwdc2019-248", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/248", "wordCount": 1161, "segments": [{"start": 6.0, "text": "Hello. Welcome to Creating a"}, {"start": 8.0, "text": "Great Accessible Reading"}, {"start": 10.0, "text": "Experience."}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "My name is Darren Minifie, and"}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "I'm an engineering manager on"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "the Accessibility Team."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "The hallmark for a great"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "application is an outstanding"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "user interface."}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "This extends to the layout and"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "styling of text especially for"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "apps whose primary focus is the"}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "presentation of long form"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "readable content."}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "To implement a custom text"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "layout you often need to turn to"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "lower level technologies such as"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "Core Text and TextKit."}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "In this session, you will learn"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "the APIs and techniques you need"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "to create an equally great"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "accessible reading experience"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "for VoiceOver."}, {"start": 47.0, "text": "We'll begin by talking about the"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "reading content protocol."}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "You use this protocol to make"}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "your text content accessible."}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "Next, we'll talk about automatic"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "page turning, which VoiceOver"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "uses to turn the pages in your"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "Finally, we'll discuss the APIs"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "you can use to customize the way"}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "VoiceOver speaks your content."}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "In the session, we'll use the"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "following sample app to"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "demonstrate these techniques."}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "The app is a simple page-based"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "application where each page"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "consists of an image, a title, a"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "subtitle and some detail text."}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "To make your app accessible, you"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "should first audit it with"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "VoiceOver."}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "A convenient way to do this is"}, {"start": 89.0, "text": "to add VoiceOver to your"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "accessibility shortcut."}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "You can do this by launching"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "settings, tapping accessibility,"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "scrolling down to accessibility"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "shortcut and tapping VoiceOver."}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "Now depending on your hardware,"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "you can press the home button or"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "side button 3 times to quickly"}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "enable and disable VoiceOver."}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "Let's see how VoiceOver"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "interacts with the sample app."}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "VoiceOver on."}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "As I drag my finger across"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "the screen, VoiceOver plays a"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "sound effect indicating there is"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "no content to be found."}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "Therefore, the first thing we"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "need to do is make our text"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "content accessible."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "To make your content accessible,"}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "you should use the"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "UIAccessibilityReadingContent"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "Protocol."}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "This protocol consists of 4 core"}, {"start": 137.0, "text": "methods."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "AccessibilityLineNumber(for"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "point asks you to return the"}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "line number for a given touch"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "location."}, {"start": 144.0, "text": "AccessibilityContent"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "(forLineNumber and"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "accessibilityFrame"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "(forLineNumber asks for the text"}, {"start": 150.0, "text": "content and rect for a given"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "line respectively."}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "Finally, accessibilityPageContent asks"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "you to return the entire pages"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "worth of content."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "Let's see how we would implement"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "the UIAccessibilityReadingContent"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "Protocol in our sample app."}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "Each page in the sample app is"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "represented by an instance of"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "SessionItemView."}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "This view has 4 sub views; an"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "image view, a title label, an"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "identifier label and a session"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "details view."}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "We additionally declare a layout"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "enum."}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "This will help us in our method"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "implementations that follow."}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "The first thing we need to do is"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "make our page view an"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "accessibility element."}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "We do this by setting"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "isAccessibilityElement to true"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "in the page views initializer."}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "Next, we begin to implement the"}, {"start": 203.0, "text": "reading content protocol."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "Our first method is"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "accessibilityLineNumber(for"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "point."}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "First, we hitTest the page view"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "using the past in line number."}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "If the resulting view is one of"}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "our known sub views, we map that"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "to the value of our layout enum."}, {"start": 221.0, "text": "Finally, we return the rawValue"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "as this is the representation"}, {"start": 224.0, "text": "VoiceOver understands."}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "Next to implement AccessibilityContent"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "(forLineNumber, we begin by"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "instantiating an instance of the"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "layout enum."}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "We switch over the possible"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "cases and map that to one of our"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "known sub views."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "Finally, we return accessibility"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "label, which returns the text"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "for that sub view."}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "The implementation of"}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "accessibilityFrame"}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "(forLineNumber is very similar."}, {"start": 252.0, "text": "We begin by creating a new"}, {"start": 254.0, "text": "instance of the layout enum with"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "our given raw value."}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "We switch over the possible"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "cases and map that to one of our"}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "known sub views."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "Finally, we return accessibility"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "frame, which represents the rect"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "for a given line."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "Finally, to implement"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "accessibilityPageContent we"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "gather together the text from"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "our known sub views and return"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "them as a single string."}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "Let's see how the app interacts"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "with VoiceOver with the reading"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "content protocol implemented."}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "Accessible drag-and-drop."}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "Session 241."}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "Drag-and-drop is a powerful API"}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "that allows apps to share and"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "communicate data."}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "This time as I drag my finger"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "across the screen VoiceOver"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "speaks and highlights the"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "corresponding text."}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "Next let's talk about automatic"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "page turning."}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "When VoiceOver's read all"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "command is invoked, it's"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "expected that VoiceOver will be"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "able to read all of your content"}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "from beginning to end."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "This may require VoiceOver to"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "turn pages in your app."}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "To implement automatic page"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "turning you need to adopt 2"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "accessibility APIs."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "First, you should include the"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "causesPageTurn accessibility"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "trait on your page view."}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "Second, you should implement"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "AccessibilityScroll in"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "direction."}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "This gives VoiceOver the ability"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "to turn pages in your app."}, {"start": 337.0, "text": "Let's see how we would implement"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "automatic page turning in our"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "sample app."}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "First, we need to include the"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "causesPageTurn accessibility"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "trait. We do this by setting"}, {"start": 348.0, "text": "accessibility trait in the page"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "views initializer."}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "Next, we implement"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "accessibilityScroll and"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "direction."}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "We do this by switching over the"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "possible cases of the direction"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "parameter."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "If the direction is previous or"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "left, we ask our delegate to"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "turn to the previous page."}, {"start": 367.0, "text": "If that's successful, we notify"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "VoiceOver with a pageScrolled"}, {"start": 370.0, "text": "notification."}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "Similarly, if the value is right"}, {"start": 376.0, "text": "or next, we ask the delegate to"}, {"start": 378.0, "text": "turn to the next page and if"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "that's successful, we notify"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "VoiceOver with a pageScrolled"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "notification."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "Let's see how the app interacts"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "with automatic page turning"}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "implemented."}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "Accessible drag-and-drop"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "Session 241."}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "Drag-and-drop is a powerful API"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "that allows apps to share and"}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "communicate data."}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "No matter how you decide to"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "implant drag-and-drop there's a"}, {"start": 401.0, "text": "way to make it work for people"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "with accessibility needs."}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "Learn the details as we dive"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "into accessible drag-and-drop"}, {"start": 406.0, "text": "for iOS."}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "AVSpeechSynthesizer."}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "Making iOS talk."}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "Session 236."}, {"start": 413.0, "text": "Our final topic is"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "customizing speech."}, {"start": 417.0, "text": "You may want to control the way"}, {"start": 419.0, "text": "VoiceOver speaks your app's"}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 421.0, "text": "To do this you can use 2"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "alternate methods in the reading"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "content protocol."}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "These method versions return"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "NSAttributedStrings instead of"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "simple strings."}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "By supplying the appropriate"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "accessibility attributes, you"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "can control various aspects"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "about how VoiceOver speaks your"}, {"start": 437.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "For example, you may have a"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "passage you would like spoken in"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "a particular language."}, {"start": 444.0, "text": "To do this you can include the"}, {"start": 446.0, "text": "accessibilitySpeechLanguage"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "attribute along with the"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "appropriate language identifier."}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "This causes VoiceOver to use the"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "most appropriate voice to speak"}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "your content."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "Arc de Triomphe."}, {"start": 460.0, "text": "Furthermore, you may want"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "fine-grained control over the"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "way VoiceOver speaks your"}, {"start": 464.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "To do this you can supply the"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "IPA representation for your"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "passage along with the"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "accessibilitySpeechIPANotation"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "attribute."}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "Yosemite National Park."}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "So to create a great reading"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "experience for VoiceOver, you"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "first need to make your text"}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "content accessible."}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "You do this by implementing the"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "UIAccessibilityReadingContent"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "protocol."}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "Next, you should implement"}, {"start": 492.0, "text": "automatic page turning so"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "VoiceOver can read all of the"}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "content in your app from"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "beginning to end."}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "Finally, to control the way"}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "VoiceOver speaks your content,"}, {"start": 502.0, "text": "you should consider using the NS"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "attributed strings versions of"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "the methods in the reading"}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "content protocol and supply the"}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "appropriate accessibility"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "attributes."}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "For more information about this"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "topic, please visit the"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "following session URL."}]}